    "uid": "430981a778227c19cf2e8a7f0f2f6e55",
    "title": "Suspicious PowerShell encoded command",
    "desc": "PowerShell launched with an encoded command and hiding flags - the classic fileless launcher / download-cradle shape. This is banken's first Windows (Sysmon) detection, and it exists to prove the Sysmon source end to end: it keys on the same process_creation fields a SigmaHQ Windows rule uses (Image, CommandLine), which the Sysmon parser fills from a Windows Event Log record exactly as the auditd parser fills them from a Linux exec. So SigmaHQ's whole Windows ruleset drops in the same way. See docs/windows.md for the scaffold status (logsource-aware routing is the next piece, so until then a Windows rule simply never matches a Linux event by field shape).",
